          "upper": null,
          "infinite": "true",
          "description": "The summarized EventId definition record consists of a summarized event ID and specific Dem Events.",
          "metadata": {
            "INTRODUCTION": "This record means that a particular FID that has to be disabled in case of summarized event (defined above) is to be disabled in any of the specific events. A possible solution could be assigning events as summarized events along with a list of specific events. During the configuration process the summarized event substitutes the referenced single events. However, it is not outlined how this requirement is solved - whether by configuration process or by implementation within the FiM. The FiM configuration tool could also build up a suitable data structure for summarized events and deal with it in the FiM implementation.",
